## Contract (checked automatically)
- Write `void mainAudio(out vec4 o, in float t)` plus any helper functions. `t` = seconds from the start of the demo{% if spec.loop %} (already wrapped modulo the duration){% endif %}. Stereo output: `o.x` = left, `o.y` = right, in [-1, 1]; `o.z`, `o.w` are ignored.
- Available: `#define BPM`, `uniform float iSampleRate`. Derive the rhythm from `t` only:
  `float beatDur = 60.0 / BPM; float beat = floor(t / beatDur); float ph = fract(t / beatDur);`
  `float bar = floor(beat / {{ spec.timeline.beats_per_bar }}.0);` — do NOT use iTime, uBeat, uBeatPhase, uBar (they are per audio block, not per sample).
- Library functions already available (do NOT redefine them):
{{ library }}
- You can also write your own voices: sine `sin(6.2831853*f*t)`, saw `fract(f*t)*2.0-1.0`, square `sign(sin(...))`, envelopes `exp(-k*dt)`, filters by mixing, chords by summing notes `f = 55.0*pow(2.0, semi/12.0)`.
- Rhythm: drum hits must start exactly on the beat grid (time since hit = `ph * beatDur`, or offsets of beatDur/2, beatDur/4): mean onset error must stay under {{ max_onset_ms }} ms.
- Loudness: never silent except an intro/outro of at most 2 bars; keep the mix around 0.6-0.8 peak and finish with a soft clip `s = tanh(s)` (no hard clipping at 1.0).
- Cost: this runs for EVERY sample (~44100 per second): at least {{ min_realtime }}x faster than realtime is required. No loops over 8 iterations, no raymarching, at most ~6-8 voices.
- Deterministic: randomness only from `hash11` of the sample index.
- GLSL ES 3.00: float literals with a dot (1.0), no implicit int/float conversions, no recursion, no textures.

